Task 1: Study OpenShift Virtualization Architecture
Subtask 1.1: Understanding the Overall Architecture
OpenShift Virtualization extends OpenShift Container Platform to run and manage virtual machine workloads alongside container workloads.

Key Architecture Components:

OpenShift Virtualization Operator: Manages the lifecycle of virtualization components
KubeVirt: The core virtualization technology
Containerized Data Importer (CDI): Handles VM disk image imports
Multus CNI: Provides additional network interfaces
Node Feature Discovery (NFD): Detects hardware features
